over its impressive 17 seasons and  counting ncis has stood atop the police  procedural mountain the long-running  series has a serious knack for not only  making the crime drama stories important  but also giving its principal cast fully  realized backstories  one of the few drawbacks to this is that  now and again issues arise regarding  minor character details that leave fans  scratching their heads  one of the main characters of ncis is  leroy jethro gibbs  he's the no-nonsense leader of the major  case response team with a backlog of  experience in both the military and as  an nis  special agent these credentials are part  of what made gibbs such an effective  boss and he was often touted by his  co-workers as the most  capable and accomplished of them all in  the ncis universe gibbs began his  military training in 1976 right after he  graduated high school  he later served as a member of the  united states military police corps  before taking part in operation  just cause and operation desert storm  before his honorable  discharge in 1992 such a resume is  nothing to sniff at but there's one  aspect of gibb's past as a marine that's  causing something of a stir amongst the  ncis faithful  gibbs left his marine life behind after  killing mexican cartel leader pedro  hernandez the man responsible for the  death of his wife and daughter  despite the circumstances of gibb's  departure some ncis fans feel it's a bit  odd that after 16 years in the service  he stayed in the rank of gunnery  sergeant above staff sergeant and below  first sergeant and master sergeant  one viewer in particular has wondered  why gibbs didn't do a little more  climbing in the ranks before he cycled  out of the core  a reddit user posed the question i've  probably seen every ncis and now i watch  reruns  gibbs was a gunny sergeant in the  marines with his talent and leadership  skills why didn't he earn a higher rank  in response another redditor noted that  perhaps gibbs didn't move up from the  rank of gunnery sergeant because of what  happened with his family that caused him  to resign early  it's been a long time since the gibbs  flashbacks were a big part of the show  if i'm remembering everything correctly  i'd say he probably left the marines  after his family were killed  either finished his current enlistment  or was granted an early out for hardship  on the flip side there's a chance that  gibbs felt happy accomplished and  fulfilled  being a gunny that's not a far-fetched  theory in the least as the rank comes  with a great deal of responsibility  according to military.com the gunnery  sergeant rank is  considered the backbone of the marine  corps staff nco ranks  the site goes on to say marine corps  gunnery sergeants are expected to bring  their years of experience to bear in  quick  accurate decisions that are in the best  interest of the mission and their  marines  gunnery sergeants quote set the example  of leadership and professionalism for  their subordinates and must ensure that  work areas and facilities are up to  standard  equipment is maintained their  subordinates are following orders and  the day-to-day unit operation runs  smoothly in accordance to senior  officers policies  i am gunnery sergeant hartman your  senior drill instructor  from now on you will speak only when  spoken to  another possible reason why gibbs didn't  move up from gunnery sergeant to master  sergeant or first sergeant  is because it takes many years to even  reach the gunnery sergeant rank  one real-life marine noted that it took  them just over 12 years to become a  gunny  for another it took 13 years a redditor  wrote in response to the initial  question  gibbs left the core after 16 years the  average time to attain the rank of  gunnery sergeant is almost 15 years  if gibbs became a gunnery sergeant  somewhere between his 12th and his 15th  year in the core  there wouldn't have been much time to  advance whatever the case may be gibbs  continued to prove his skills post  marines becoming the ncis  special agent fans know and love today i  must fire my rifle  true check out one of our newest videos  right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

